  "goodToKnow": "Die Weltliteratur is world literature, the great works read across cultures. Goethe popularised the term in conversations with Eckermann in 1827, hoping national literatures would give way to an exchange between nations. German contributions include Goethe's Faust, Kafka's Der Process and Thomas Mann's Der Zauberberg. German-language Nobel laureates include Thomas Mann, Heinrich Böll, Günter Grass and Herta Müller. It has no plural."
